From a9a79059fc4a3bf7d93920d478f9b9ca93941bfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <mia.ailab1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:54:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 35/63] glm cuda: TF_GLM_CE_EXCHANGE=1 pushes a prompt chunk's
 split exchanges by copy engines

With two ranks on one host and the direct split (the default), TF_GLM_CE_EXCHANGE=1 replaces each piece's
splitPartials and splitGlued send/recv pairs: each rank copies its rows (cuMemcpyDtoDAsync in TF_GLM_CE_CHUNK_KB
pieces, 1024) straight into the peer's room or glued rows, mapped through CUDA IPC at startup by role (rooms, normed,
hidden), then writes the next sequence number into the peer's flag line with cuStreamWriteValue32 (fenced after the
copies); the side stream waits for its own flag with cuStreamWaitValue32 before the glue. The bytes land where NCCL
put them, so the bits are unchanged, and no SMs run the exchange. A batched pass of several fresh prompts (prefillMany) takes
the same path on the same prompt buffers and pieces.

Pieces carries ce_slot0 so a paired chunk's twin Pieces (#1423) can take its own flag slots; a twin buffer set
registers its roles in the same order. Off by default until measured; both ranks always meet in the setup exchange.

Measured: copy engines move 26.4 GB/s a direction both ways at once (1 MiB copies) against NCCL send/recv's 20.6-22.8
at the 3 and 6 MiB piece sizes.

